{"id": "EUVD-2026-93320", "enisaUuid": "129d21ed-6e30-3034-bd1f-dca4156b7ddd", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: mac80211: abort chanswitch when leaving a mesh\n\nThe code in ieee80211_stop_mesh() leaves CSA active, but leaving\nthe mesh released the channel context, so the CSA finalize work\ncrashes:\n\n  Oops: general protection fault, probably for non-canonical address\n        0xdffffc0000000003\n  KASAN: null-ptr-deref in range [0x0000000000000018-0x000000000000001f]\n  RIP: 0010:ieee80211_put_srates_elem+0x42/0x640 net/mac80211/util.c:3272\n  Call Trace:\n   ieee80211_mesh_build_beacon+0xa83/0x1b50 net/mac80211/mesh.c:1093\n   ieee80211_mesh_rebuild_beacon+0xc7/0x170 net/mac80211/mesh.c:1147\n   ieee80211_mesh_finish_csa+0x131/0x210 net/mac80211/mesh.c:1542\n   ieee80211_set_after_csa_beacon net/mac80211/cfg.c:4085 [inline]\n   __ieee80211_csa_finalize net/mac80211/cfg.c:4133 [inline]\n   ieee80211_csa_finalize+0x633/0x1150 net/mac80211/cfg.c:4155\n   cfg80211_wiphy_work+0x2ab/0x450 net/wireless/core.c:438\n\nAbort the channel switch properly.", "datePublished": "2026-10-06T08:46:26", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:17:46", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bc544ef02327edf61c94d2b6bae9d14b217009b2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2e1d6e80148495e728a85a9250176f266312e55c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d222fdc973bb8dbf0357772bd9042ffdc8291939", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ac7472a24bd433b81c06582835dd1d5547c10da9"], "aliases": ["GHSA-wmxc-8xr9-g2qr", "CVE-2026-98335"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "04f58c2a-e7a8-3529-a690-645394cb3379", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "40d47ac5-2c35-349b-9c70-6ca163204d71", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "50c49deb-3683-3d48-b36f-0fe50beca4fc", "product": {"name":